The '''Czinger 21C''' is a hybrid sports car developed using 3D printing<ref name="r&t">{{cite journal |last1=Stevens |first1=Tim |title=The Real Value of 3D Printing |journal=[[Road & Track]] |date=January 2023 |volume=14 |page=22|url=https://www.roadandtrack.com/car-culture/a42396407/the-real-value-of-3d-printing/|url-access=subscription}}</ref> by the American car manufacturer [[Czinger]] Vehicles. Manufacturing began in 2021,<ref>{{cite web|title=Czinger 21C Hybride : une hypercar de 1233 chevaux|url=https://www.turbo.fr/actualite-automobile/czinger-21c-hybride-une-hypercar-de-1233-chevaux-157597|author=Jean-Etienne Celle|date=17 February 2020|publication-date=}}</ref> with a planned production run of 80 units and deliveries starting Q4 2023, most expected to be delivered in 2024 according to founder Kevin Czinger.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Pequeño IV |first=Antonio |date=2022-06-27 |title=Czinger Vehicles Establishes Dealer Network |url=https://labusinessjournal.com/featured/czinger-vehicles-establishes-dealer-network/ |access-date=2024-10-19 |website=[[Los Angeles Business Journal]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

==Presentation==
Designed, developed and built in [[Los Angeles]], [[California]], the Czinger 21C launched the new brand Czinger Vehicles<ref>{{cite web|title=1250 chevaux pour la Czinger 21C|url=https://www.endurance-info.com/fr/1250-chevaux-pour-la-czinger-21c/|author=claudeenduranceinfocom|website=www.endurance-info.com|date=17 February 2020|access-date=19 February 2020|publication-date=}}</ref> named after its founders Kevin and Lukas Czinger. The car was to be presented at the [[Geneva Motor Show]] in March 2020, but the show was canceled due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Le Salon de l'automobile de Genève est annulé|url=https://www.tdg.ch/suisse/conseil-federal-interdit-manifestations-mille-personnes/story/19591038|author=Virginie Lenk|date=28 February 2020|publication-date=|access-date=29 February 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200327231100/https://www.tdg.ch/suisse/conseil-federal-interdit-manifestations-mille-personnes/story/19591038|archive-date=27 March 2020|url-status=dead}}</ref> It was instead presented on March 11, 2020, in [[London]] during a special event.<ref>{{cite web|title=Czinger 21C : la voiture du futur peut faire encore rêver|url=https://www.caradisiac.com/czinger-21c-la-voiture-du-futur-peut-faire-encore-rever-181921.htm|author=Pierre Desjardins|date=12 March 2020|publication-date=}}</ref>

Czinger Vehicles will produce only 80 units in two configurations: a road variant and a track variant called "Lightweight Track".<ref>{{cite web|title=Salon de Genève 2020 : la nouvelle marque Czinger avec la supercar 21C|url=https://www.caradisiac.com/salon-de-geneve-2020-la-nouvelle-marque-czinger-avec-la-supercar-21c-181489.htm|author=Audric Doche|date=21 February 2020|publication-date=}}</ref>

==Technical characteristics==
The 21C has a driver's seat in the central position and an in-line, tandem passenger seat behind that of the driver, minimizing the width of the cockpit.<ref>{{cite web|title=Czinger 21C (2020) : 1.250ch pour la supercar imprimée en 3D|url=https://news.sportauto.fr/news/1546554/Czinger-21C-impression-3D-vid%C3%A9o-salon-Gen%C3%A8ve-2020|author=Maxime K|website=news.sportauto.fr|date=17 February 2020|access-date=19 February 2020|publication-date=|archive-date=19 February 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200219084426/https://news.sportauto.fr/news/1546554/Czinger-21C-impression-3D-vid%25C3%25A9o-salon-Gen%25C3%25A8ve-2020|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Golson |first=Daniel |title=Czinger 21C First Ride Review: 3D-Printed Absurdity |url=https://www.cnet.com/roadshow/news/czinger-21c-hypercar-first-ride-review-3d-printed-divergent-manufacturing/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240519193127/https://www.cnet.com/roadshow/news/czinger-21c-hypercar-first-ride-review-3d-printed-divergent-manufacturing/ |archive-date=2024-05-19 |access-date=2024-06-27 |website=CNET |language=en}}</ref>

The brake caliper and [[Steering knuckle|upright]] components are combined into a single unit called the BrakeNode.<ref name="r&t"/><ref name="SAE_auto_engr">{{Cite magazine |last=Dinkel |first=John |date=August 2023 |title=3D, No Waiting! Two companies’ latest techniques take additive manufacturing to the next level |url=https://www.nxtbook.com/smg/sae/23AE08/index.php#/p/16 |magazine=[[SAE International|Automotive Engineering]] |pages=16-19 |issn=2331-7647}}</ref>

==Powertrain==
The 21C has a hybrid gasoline engine consisting of a bespoke [[Flat-plane crank]] twin-turbo V8 of {{convert|2.88|L|cuin|sp=us}} capacity, has a bore x stroke of {{convert|84|x|65|mm|2|abbr=on}} in the rear central position associated with two electric motors located on the front and powered by a [[lithium-titanate battery]]. The combination provides {{convert|1,250|hp|kW PS|0}} at 10,500 rpm transmitted to the rear wheels via a seven-speed sequential transaxle with hydraulic actuated multi-plate clutch.<ref>{{cite web|title=Czinger 21C: les détails|url=https://www.asphalte.ch/news/2020/02/czinger-21c-les-details/2/|author=J-C Etter|date=21 February 2020|publication-date=}}</ref> An exclusive version limited to 4 examples called the 21C Blackbird increases the power output to {{convert|1350|hp|kW PS}} by tuning the engine for 101 octane fuel.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Driven: 2025 Czinger 21C V Max, a Fighter Jet for the Road |url=https://www.caranddriver.com/reviews/a69076019/2025-czinger-21c-v-max-drive/ |website=Car and Driver}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=H.R. Owen Delivers First Customer Czinger 21C Blackbird Edition |url=https://www.hrowen.co.uk/czinger/news/h-r-owen-delivers-first-customer-czinger-21c-blackbird-edition/ |website=H. R. Owen}}</ref>

